From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] drm: allow dumb buffer ioctls on render nodes

Android's minigbm gralloc opens the DRM render node and allocates with
DRM_IOCTL_MODE_CREATE_DUMB when the GPU has no 3D path (virtio-gpu in 2D
mode under QEMU; also a fallback for display-only KMS drivers). Upstream
only allows the dumb ioctls on the primary node, so the allocator fails
with EACCES and SurfaceFlinger aborts with "output buffer not gpu
writeable" (Build 069 M3, boot 5).

This is the same change the Android Common Kernel carries as
"ANDROID: Allow DRM_IOCTL_MODE_*_DUMB for render clients" (b/123764798,
used by Cuttlefish without 3D). Not suitable for upstream.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/20180724082213.25677-1-robert.foss@collabora.com/
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_ioctl.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_ioctl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_ioctl.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_ioctl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_ioctl.c
@@ -680,7 +680,7 @@
	DRM_IOCTL_DEF(DRM_IOCTL_MODE_PAGE_FLIP, drm_mode_page_flip_ioctl, DRM_MASTER),
	DRM_IOCTL_DEF(DRM_IOCTL_MODE_DIRTYFB, drm_mode_dirtyfb_ioctl, DRM_MASTER),
-	DRM_IOCTL_DEF(DRM_IOCTL_MODE_CREATE_DUMB, drm_mode_create_dumb_ioctl, 0),
-	DRM_IOCTL_DEF(DRM_IOCTL_MODE_MAP_DUMB, drm_mode_mmap_dumb_ioctl, 0),
-	DRM_IOCTL_DEF(DRM_IOCTL_MODE_DESTROY_DUMB, drm_mode_destroy_dumb_ioctl, 0),
+	DRM_IOCTL_DEF(DRM_IOCTL_MODE_CREATE_DUMB, drm_mode_create_dumb_ioctl, DRM_RENDER_ALLOW),
+	DRM_IOCTL_DEF(DRM_IOCTL_MODE_MAP_DUMB, drm_mode_mmap_dumb_ioctl, DRM_RENDER_ALLOW),
+	DRM_IOCTL_DEF(DRM_IOCTL_MODE_DESTROY_DUMB, drm_mode_destroy_dumb_ioctl, DRM_RENDER_ALLOW),
	DRM_IOCTL_DEF(DRM_IOCTL_MODE_OBJ_GETPROPERTIES, drm_mode_obj_get_properties_ioctl, 0),
	DRM_IOCTL_DEF(DRM_IOCTL_MODE_OBJ_SETPROPERTY, drm_mode_obj_set_property_ioctl, DRM_MASTER),
